# Documentation Structure Rules

## Directory Organization

### Main Structure
```
Docs/
├── Meetings/           # Meeting notes and session records
├── Planning/           # Game design documents and specifications
├── Architecture/       # Technical architecture documents
├── API/               # API documentation and technical references
└── Assets/            # Documentation-related assets (images, diagrams)
```

### File Naming Convention
- **Format**: `YYYYMMDD_Category_Title.md`
- **Examples**:
  - `20250525_ArmoredFrame_Architecture.md`
  - `20250526_GameDesign_CombatSystem.md`
  - `20250527_API_EventBusReference.md`

## Document Categories

### Meetings (`Docs/Meetings/`)
- **Purpose**: Session records, decision logs, progress tracking
- **Content**: Agenda, attendees, decisions, action items, next steps
- **Format**: Structured markdown with consistent headers

### Planning (`Docs/Planning/`)
- **Purpose**: Game design documents, feature specifications
- **Content**: Game mechanics, user stories, feature requirements
- **Format**: Detailed specifications with examples and mockups

### Architecture (`Docs/Architecture/`)
- **Purpose**: Technical design documents, system overviews
- **Content**: System diagrams, code structure, design patterns
- **Format**: Technical documentation with code examples

### API (`Docs/API/`)
- **Purpose**: Code documentation, usage guides, references
- **Content**: Class references, method documentation, usage examples
- **Format**: Auto-generated or manually maintained API docs

## Documentation Standards

### Markdown Structure
```markdown
# Document Title

**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
**Author:** [Author Name]
**Status:** [Draft/Review/Approved]

---

## Overview
[Brief description]

## Content Sections
[Main content with clear headers]

---

**Next Steps:** [If applicable]
**Related Documents:** [Cross-references]
```

### Content Guidelines
- Use clear, descriptive headings (H1-H4)
- Include table of contents for long documents
- Add cross-references between related documents
- Include code examples with proper syntax highlighting
- Use bullet points and numbered lists for clarity

## Version Control

### Document Status
- **Draft**: Work in progress, not finalized
- **Review**: Ready for review, pending approval
- **Approved**: Finalized and officially adopted
- **Archived**: Outdated but kept for reference

### Update Protocol
- Always update modification date when editing
- Maintain changelog for significant documents
- Archive old versions when major revisions occur
- Cross-link related documents when updating

## Responsibility Matrix

### SASHA (Documentation Manager)
- Create and maintain document templates
- Ensure consistent formatting and structure
- Generate meeting notes and technical documentation
- Maintain cross-references and document organization

### Woochang (Content Approver)
- Review and approve all documentation
- Provide technical content and specifications
- Make final decisions on document structure changes
- Validate technical accuracy of documentation

## Quality Assurance

### Review Checklist
- [ ] Proper file naming convention followed
- [ ] Document structure matches template
- [ ] All technical information is accurate
- [ ] Cross-references are valid and up-to-date
- [ ] Language is clear and concise
- [ ] Code examples are tested and working

### Maintenance Schedule
- **Weekly**: Review and update active documents
- **Monthly**: Archive outdated documents
- **Quarterly**: Review overall documentation structure
- **As needed**: Update templates and standards

